2026-11-07T07:09:41.6012930Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6047520Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6048070Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6048410Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6048560Z 
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6048730Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6048910Z 
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6049060Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6049390Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6049540Z 
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6049620Z If you would like to
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6049870Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6050050Z 
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6050170Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6051110Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-07T07:09:41.6051230Z 
